{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.YoungIdempotent","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.YoungIdempotent","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Fin","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.YoungIdempotent.youngSym3_eigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.YoungIdempotent.youngSym3_eigenvalue","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/YoungIdempotent.lean#L177-L181","doc":"Per-instance form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.YoungIdempotent.YoungSym3Eigenvalue.eigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.YoungIdempotent.YoungSym3Eigenvalue.eigenvalue","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/YoungIdempotent.lean#L174-L174","doc":"For every generator `i`, the symmetric idempotent acts as\nmultiplication by `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.YoungIdempotent.YoungSym3Eigenvalue.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.YoungIdempotent.YoungSym3Eigenvalue.mk","kind":"ctor","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/YoungIdempotent.lean#L171-L171","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.YoungIdempotent.YoungSym3Eigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.YoungIdempotent.YoungSym3Eigenvalue","kind":"class","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/YoungIdempotent.lean#L164-L175","doc":"**Young-symmetric eigenvalue — typeclass (Pattern 4).**\n\nWitnesses the symmetric-rep eigenvalue property `σ_i · e_{(3)} = q · e_{(3)}`\nfor a *specific* representation `ρ`. The universal claim\nrequires expanding σ_i · T_w via Hecke/braid relations across\nthe full S_3 sum; until that is mechanised, callers supply a\nper-`ρ` witness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.YoungIdempotent.youngSymIdempotent2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.YoungIdempotent.youngSymIdempotent2","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/YoungIdempotent.lean#L137-L141","doc":"General Young symmetric idempotent for H₂(q):\n`e_{(2)} = I + q · T₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.YoungIdempotent.youngSymIdempotent3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.YoungIdempotent.youngSymIdempotent3","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/YoungIdempotent.lean#L115-L135","doc":"The Young symmetric idempotent evaluated in a representation.\n\nFor a representation ρ : H_n(q) → End(V), the image of the\nYoung symmetric idempotent is:\n\n`ρ(e_{(n)}) = ∑_{w ∈ S_n} q^{ℓ(w)} · ρ(T_w)`\n\nwhere `T_w` is the Hecke algebra element for permutation w\n(using any reduced word).\n\nFor H₃(q), this is explicitly:\n`e_{(3)} = 1 + q·T₁ + q·T₂ + q²·T₁T₂ + q²·T₂T₁ + q³·T₁T₂T₁` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.YoungIdempotent.poincarePolynomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.YoungIdempotent.poincarePolynomial","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/YoungIdempotent.lean#L94-L109","doc":"The Poincaré polynomial `P_n(q²) = ∑_{w ∈ S_n} q^{2ℓ(w)}`.\n\nThis is the sum of `q^{2ℓ(w)}` over all permutations in S_n.\nIt equals the q²-factorial: `P_n(q²) = [n]_{q²}!`.\n\nRecursion: `P_n = P_{n-1} · [n]_{q²}` where\n`[n]_{q²} = 1 + q² + q⁴ + … + q^{2(n-1)}`.\n\nFor small n:\n- P₁ = 1\n- P₂ = 1 + q² = [2]_{q²}\n- P₃ = (1 + q²)(1 + q² + q⁴) = [2]_{q²} · [3]_{q²}\n     = 1 + 2q² + 2q⁴ + q⁶ ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.YoungIdempotent.qSqInt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.YoungIdempotent.qSqInt","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/YoungIdempotent.lean#L83-L92","doc":"The q²-integer `[n]_{q²} = 1 + q² + q⁴ + … + q^{2(n−1)}`\nas an element of `ℤ[t, t⁻¹]` where `q = t²`.\n\nThis is the sum form — no division required, so it lives in\nthe Laurent polynomial ring directly.\n\n`[n]_{q²} = Σ_{k=0}^{n-1} q^{2k} = Σ_{k=0}^{n-1} t^{4k}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.YoungIdempotent.S3_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.YoungIdempotent.S3_card","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/YoungIdempotent.lean#L78-L79","doc":"The number of elements in S₃. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.YoungIdempotent.S3_reduced_words","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.YoungIdempotent.S3_reduced_words","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/YoungIdempotent.lean#L58-L76","doc":"The 6 elements of S₃ as permutations of Fin 3, with their\nCoxeter lengths and reduced words.\n\n| Element | Cycle notation | Length | Reduced word |\n|---------|---------------|--------|--------------|\n| e       | ()            | 0      | []           |\n| s₀      | (0 1)         | 1      | [0]          |\n| s₁      | (1 2)         | 1      | [1]          |\n| s₀s₁    | (0 1 2)       | 2      | [0, 1]       |\n| s₁s₀    | (0 2 1)       | 2      | [1, 0]       |\n| s₀s₁s₀  | (0 2)         | 3      | [0, 1, 0]    |\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.YoungIdempotent.coxeterLength_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.YoungIdempotent.coxeterLength_one","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/YoungIdempotent.lean#L48-L54","doc":"The identity permutation has length 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.YoungIdempotent.coxeterLength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.YoungIdempotent.coxeterLength","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/YoungIdempotent.lean#L42-L46","doc":"The Coxeter length of a permutation: the number of inversions.\n`ℓ(w) = #{(i, j) : i < j ∧ w(i) > w(j)}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}